  "text": "חבל\n\n\\Column{\n\\subsection{Step 1: Find the roots of the denominator of the right-hand side}\nThe denominator of the right-hand side is a cubic polynomial. Let's find its roots using a substitution.\n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - 120x^2 + 2718x - 32400 &= 0 \\\\\nx^3 - 10x^2 - 220x^2 + 2718x - 32400 &= 0 \\\\\nx^3 - 10x^2 + 2718x - 32400 &= 0\n\\end{align*}\nNow we can use the substitution $y = x^2$:\n\\[ y^2 - 10y + 2nd-ay - 32400 = 0 \\]\nSolving for $y$ using the quadratic formula:\n\\[ y = 460, \\quad y = 60 \\]\nThus, the roots of the cubic polynomial are:\n\\[ x = \\sqrt{460}, \\quad x = \\sqrt{60}, \\quad x = -10 \\]\n\\Column[\n\\subsection{Step 2: Find the corresponding roots of the left-hand side}\nNow we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy the left-hand side: $\\frac{x+\\alpha}{x-\\beta} = 0$.\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{x+\\alpha}{x-\\beta} &= 0 \\\\\nx+\\alpha &= 0 \\\\\nx &= -\\alpha\n\\end{align*}\nFor $x = -\\alpha$ to be a root of the left-hand side, we must have:\n\\[ -\\alpha \\neq \\beta \\]\n\n\\Column[\n\\subsection{Step 3: Find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$}\nSince the left-hand side and the right-hand side have a common root, let us denote this common root by $r$. Then:\n\\[ r = -\\alpha = \\sqrt{460}, \\quad r = \\alpha = \\sqrt{60}, \\quad r = \\alpha = -10 \\]\nColumn[\n\\subsection{Step 4: Calculate $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$}\nLet's go back to our roots of the denominators:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{roots: } & 460, \\quad 60, \\quad 10 \\\\\n\\text{common roots: } & \\sqrt{460}, \\quad \\sqrt{60}, \\quad -10\n\\end{align*}\nWe can see that $\\alpha = \\sqrt{-10}$ is not a real number, so we should check its corresponding $\\beta$:\n\n\\Column[\n\\subsection{Step 5: Calculate $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$}\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\sqrt{-10}}{r - \\beta} &= 0 \\\\\n\\sqrt{-10} &= 0 \\\\\n\\beta &= -\\sqrt{-10}\n\\end{align*}\nNow, we need to find the negative real root of the denominator, which is $-10$:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{-10}{r - \\beta} &= 0 \\\\\n-10 &= 0 \\\\\n\\beta &= -10\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore: removingColumn[\n\\subsection{Step 5: Calculate $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$}\nColumn[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\beta &= 10\n\\end{align*}\n\n\\Column[\n\\subsection{Step 6: Calculate $\\alpha \\beta$}\n\\text{Calculating the product:}\n\\begin{align*}\n\\alpha &\\beta = \\sqrt{-10} \\cdot 10 \\\\\n\\alpha &\\beta = -\\sqrt{100} \\cdot \\sqrt{10} \\\\\n\\alpha &\\beta = 10\\sqrt{-1} \\cdot \\sqrt{10} \\\\\n\\alpha &\\beta &= 10i\\sqrt{10}\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, the final answer is: $\\alpha \\beta = 106\\sqrt{-1} \\cdot \\sqrt{10} = 10\\sqrt{10}$. Column[\n\\boxed{alpha + beta",
